ditto off a Mac.

The imported dynamic framework processor archives each processed framework
with /usr/bin/ditto (-c -k --keepParent --norsrc --noextattr), which only a
Mac has. Where there is no ditto, it writes the same archive with zipfile:
the framework directory's name first, each directory before its contents,
files deflated with their permissions, symbolic links as links. bundletool
reads only the entries' names, data, executable bits and links, which match
ditto's for flat and versioned frameworks; the order is name order, where
ditto's is the Mac's file system order. A Mac still uses ditto.

--- a/tools/imported_dynamic_framework_processor/imported_dynamic_framework_processor.py
